sition as he would have been in had the contract not been made, or (c) his “restitution interest,” which is his interest in having re- stored to him any benefit that he has conferred on the other party. 1 Now § 9–109. Under the current version of Article 9, it is possible to take a security interest in a deposit account, except for consumer transactions, and many insurance claims. § 342 RESTATEMENT OF CONTRACTS—SECOND"